# Data-UI Craft — primitives kit

A small, headless-leaning set of React + Tailwind primitives that make a data-dense interface
*work*, not just look good. Generated by the `data-ui-craft` skill. Each primitive maps to one of
three pillars; swap or restyle any of them — they're intentionally thin.

## Dependencies
- **React 18+**, **Tailwind CSS** (uses utility classes incl. `tabular-nums`, `line-clamp-*`,
  `group`/`group-hover`).
- **Icons**: imported from `{{ICON_IMPORT}}` (default `lucide-react`). Swap the import if you use a
  different set.
- **`cn`**: class-merge helper imported from `{{CN}}`. If your project already has one
  (`clsx`/`tailwind-merge`/`@/lib/utils`), point imports there and delete the bundled `cn.ts`.

## What's here

### Pillar 1 — Data drives the form
| Primitive | Use for |
|---|---|
| `NumericCell` | Right-aligned, tabular, consistently formatted numbers / currency / percent. |
| `Chip` | A categorical value as a groupable shape. |
| `StatusChip` | A status value with meaningful color + dot (not color-only). Edit the `STATUS_TONE` map to your domain. |
| `TruncatedText` | Long free-text truncated *with* a reveal (tooltip or expand). |
| `DataRow` | A `<tr>` that visually de-emphasizes inactive/disabled records. |

### Pillar 2 — Progressive disclosure
| Primitive | Use for |
|---|---|
| `Popover` | Defer a medium-frequency action behind one click; focuses its primary input on open. |
| `HoverActions` | Per-row secondary actions revealed on hover/focus (visible on touch). Parent needs `className="group"`. |
| `OnboardingChecklist` | Sequenced, persisted onboarding instead of a feature-dump modal. |

### Pillar 3 — Invisible UI
| Primitive | Use for |
|---|---|
| `Tooltip` | Hover+focus tooltip. Use on every icon-only control (keep an `aria-label` too). |
| `CopyChip` | Click-to-copy for IDs/emails/keys, with copy confirmation. |
| `CommentIndicator` | Surfaces hidden comments/notes; click opens your thread panel. |
| `TableSkeleton` / `EmptyState` / `ErrorState` | The three non-happy-path states every container needs. |

## Putting it together — a row that uses all three pillars

```tsx
import {
  NumericCell, StatusChip, TruncatedText, DataRow,
  HoverActions, Tooltip, CopyChip, CommentIndicator,
  TableSkeleton, EmptyState, ErrorState,
} from "{{KIT_ROOT}}";
import { Pencil, Archive } from "{{ICON_IMPORT}}";

function UsersTable({ rows, isLoading, error, refetch }) {
  if (isLoading) return <TableSkeleton rows={6} cols={5} />;
  if (error) return <ErrorState onRetry={refetch} />;
  if (!rows.length)
    return <EmptyState title="No users yet" action={<button onClick={invite}>Invite someone</button>} />;

  return (
    <table className="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr className="text-left text-gray-500">
          <th className="px-3 py-2">Name</th>
          <th className="px-3 py-2">User ID</th>
          <th className="px-3 py-2">Status</th>
          <th className="px-3 py-2 text-right">Seats</th>{/* numeric header right-aligned too */}
          <th className="px-3 py-2" />
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((u) => (
          <DataRow key={u.id} state={u.active ? "active" : "inactive"} className="group">
            <td className="px-3 py-2">
              <TruncatedText text={u.name} />
              <CommentIndicator count={u.commentCount} onClick={() => openThread(u.id)} />
            </td>
            <td className="px-3 py-2"><CopyChip value={u.id} /></td>
            <td className="px-3 py-2"><StatusChip status={u.status} /></td>
            <td className="px-3 py-2"><NumericCell value={u.seats} /></td>
            <td className="px-3 py-2">
              <HoverActions>
                <Tooltip content="Edit"><button aria-label="Edit" className="rounded p-1 hover:bg-gray-100"><Pencil className="h-4 w-4" /></button></Tooltip>
                <Tooltip content="Archive"><button aria-label="Archive" className="rounded p-1 hover:bg-gray-100"><Archive className="h-4 w-4" /></button></Tooltip>
              </HoverActions>
            </td>
          </DataRow>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  );
}
```

The skill applies these patterns in place; the kit just saves you from re-implementing the reusable
pieces at every call site.
